#
# What a stream owes at tick `tick` of `ticks`, in Sutra (trickle_rules.h
# TK1), one stream per row: floor(total * tick / ticks) - paid in integer
# minor units (COMPUTE truncates, and nothing here is negative), the
# cumulative rule, so no period rounds a unit away. total and paid fit
# 9(12), tick and ticks 9(5); room (ticks - tick) and due are unsigned,
# so a tick past the last or a paid past what is owed is a size error,
# refused, and a ticks of 0 a division Sutra refuses. due.tb says the
# same in Trebago, which takes ticks to six digits: past 9(5) the two
# disagree and it is held.
record stream-due
  total: 9(12)
  tick: 9(5)
  ticks: 9(5)
  paid: 9(12)
  room: 9(5)
  owed: 9(12)
  due: 9(12)
procedure
  compute room = ticks - tick
  compute owed = total * tick / ticks
  compute due = owed - paid
  answer due
